# Cello Suite No. 1 in G major, BWV 1007: Menuet I (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a graceful, singing minuet in G major, slurred pairs of
# eighths and a few chords (bar 4, the last bar). Danced in a steady
# three, not hurried.
#
# Time signature: 3/4, 24 bars, no upbeat. Mutopia file bwv1007-4.mid,
# the fifth score (Prelude, Allemande, Courante, Sarabande, Menuet I):
# checked against bwv1007_menuet_i.ly. Repeat signs on both halves
# (A 1-8, B 9-24); the MIDI has no repeats, so play writes them out.
# This song is Menuet I alone, with its own repeats; Menuet II is a
# separate song (CS1MENU2), so the da capo is not played here.
#
# Range: 13 notes below B2 (the low G and D, bars 4, 8, 16, 24) are
# lifted an octave by the converter; the final G chord loses its depth.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 112 (dotted half about 37), 144 beats with repeats,
# about 1:20. Track times for Menuet I and II together (with Menuet I
# da capo): Pablo Casals (1938) 3:02 to 3:14 by transfer; Pierre
# Fournier (Archiv, 1960) 3:28. Assuming both minuets with repeats and
# the da capo without, those give about 111 to 118 (Casals) and 104
# (Fournier). The per-minuet split is my estimate, not a confirmed
# timing.
#
# Structure (score bars, my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   A  1-4    G major, the opening phrase, half close on D (4).
#      5-8    To D major, cadence (8).
#   B  9-12   D major, then toward E minor.
#      13-16  B7 to E minor, cadence (16).
#      17-20  C major and A minor sequences, A7.
#      21-24  D7 and home to G, final cadence.
#
# Bars as performed (play): A 1-8, A repeat 9-16, B 17-32 (score x =
# x+8), B repeat 33-48 (score x = x+24).

tempo 112

play 1-8 1-8 9-24 9-24

dyn 1 mf             # A, first time
dyn 9 mp             # A repeat, an echo
dyn 17 mf            # B, first time
dyn 33 mp            # B repeat, an echo
dyn 45 mf            # score 21 on: the way home, full again

rit 2 0.8            # the last two bars into the final chord
